# The first client-to-server TLS application-data record of two connections,
# captured at the wire boundary.
# produced_by: cargo test -p podnet --test cover the_first_record_of_a_switch_is_the_covers_first_record,
#   with a tee on the server socket of the local cover (127.0.0.1). The
#   handshake records are dropped before the first data record. The
#   authenticated client sends the proof and its padding; the unauthenticated
#   client sends a GET padded to the same size and receives the real page.
# produced_on: 2026-11-21
# cover_version: 1.7.2
# cover_script: tests/data/cover/script.toml
# bound: both payloads are the script's first record size, 221 application
#   bytes plus the 17-byte TLS 1.3 overhead, so 238 wire bytes (difference 0)
# label type version payload_bytes
authenticated 23 0303 238
unauthenticated 23 0303 238
